    14	/// Per-session scrollback ring held by the backend. 16 MB is enough to survive a
    15	/// genuinely long agent run (256 KB was ~2 minutes of a chatty build), and it is
    16	/// the backend that has to hold it: a hidden view holds nothing, so a re-attach
    17	/// can only replay what lives here.
    18	const TERMINAL_SCROLLBACK_MAX_BYTES: usize = 16 * 1024 * 1024;
    19	/// Hysteresis floor. Once the cap is exceeded, ONE drain takes the buffer down to
    20	/// this — 75% of the cap — instead of shaving off exactly the overflow. Trimming
    21	/// to the cap would make every subsequent 8 KB read memmove the whole 16 MB; this
    22	/// way the O(n) drain amortizes over ~4 MB of output.
    23	const TERMINAL_SCROLLBACK_TRIM_TO_BYTES: usize = TERMINAL_SCROLLBACK_MAX_BYTES / 4 * 3;
