   731	## 8. Structured/native-terminal ownership handoff
   732	
   733	### 8.1 State machine
   734	
   735	```text
   736	StructuredOwned
   737	  -> PreparingTerminal
   738	  -> TerminalOwned
   739	  -> PreparingStructured
   740	  -> StructuredOwned
   741	```
   742	
   743	`PreparingTerminal`:
   744	
   745	1. block new structured prompts;
   746	2. finish or interrupt the active turn according to user choice;
   747	3. flush normalized events and capture provider/native IDs;
   748	4. close/unsubscribe the structured writer without deleting the provider session;
   749	5. start the existing PTY with the exact native resume command;
   750	6. prove the new PTY owns the same native conversation;
   751	7. begin incremental transcript projection;
   752	8. mark terminal ownership only after the TUI is live.
   753	
   754	`PreparingStructured`:
   755	
   756	1. block PTY composer writes;
   757	2. ask the user to exit or explicitly terminate the native TUI when still active;
   758	3. stop transcript projection after the final append is processed;
   759	4. resume/load the provider session through ACP;
   760	5. import/reconcile turns added by the native TUI;
   761	6. prove native IDs and history boundary;
   762	7. acquire the structured writer lease;
   763	8. mark structured ownership.
   764	
   765	Failure rolls back to the previous usable owner. It never leaves two writers or loses the terminal scrollback.
   766	
   767	### 8.2 Fork to terminal/provider
   768	
   769	Separate actions:
   770	
   771	- **Open in native CLI** transfers the same conversation;
   772	- **Fork to native CLI** creates a new provider-native branch and leaves the structured source open;
   773	- **Fork with provider…** creates a new Assembly session with copied bounded context and a selected provider/model; it is not claimed as the same provider thread.
   774	
   775	### 8.3 Codex shared app-server optimization
   776	
   777	A later Codex-specific spike may connect both Assembly and the Codex TUI to one app-server daemon using the TUI’s remote endpoint support. This is an optimization only after proving:
   778	
   779	- one thread identity;
   780	- one active writer lease;
   781	- exact subscription/unsubscription behavior;
   782	- no duplicate rollout;
   783	- approvals and settings remain synchronized;
   784	- clean disconnect/reconnect.
   785	
   786	The first implementation does not depend on this optimization.
   787	
