  1629	## 15. Persistence, recovery, security, and trust boundaries
  1630	
  1631	### 15.1 Sources of truth
  1632	
  1633	```text
  1634	Provider conversation/context
  1635	  Provider/ACP session storage and native transcript.
  1636	
  1637	Assembly normalized conversation journal
  1638	  Rebuildable projection/audit for UI continuity; not the provider context authority.
  1639	
  1640	Owned session/workspace state
  1641	  Existing versioned local persistence keyed by ownedId.
  1642	
  1643	Workflow runs
  1644	  Existing append-only orchestration ledger plus deterministic reducer.
  1645	
  1646	Usage analytics
  1647	  Append-only normalized usage events plus rebuildable aggregate cache.
  1648	```
  1649	
  1650	### 15.2 Recovery
  1651	
  1652	On app restart:
  1653	
  1654	1. reconcile owned sessions and surviving PTYs;
  1655	2. restore workspace snapshots without starting providers merely because rows exist;
  1656	3. reattach structured runtimes only for sessions that were active/running and whose provider supports resume/load;
  1657	4. restore terminal projections for surviving PTYs;
  1658	5. replay workflow ledger and mark indeterminate running nodes as recovering;
  1659	6. query provider session state before retrying work;
  1660	7. never rerun a possibly-completed consequential action without deterministic revalidation and user-visible outcome-unknown state.
  1661	
  1662	### 15.3 Secrets
  1663	
  1664	Never persist or expose through conversation/workflow/usage/browser telemetry:
  1665	
  1666	- provider tokens/API keys;
  1667	- cookies/local storage/form values;
  1668	- full process environments;
  1669	- GitHub auth headers/tokens;
  1670	- keychain values;
  1671	- arbitrary provider stderr containing secrets;
  1672	- complete remote HTML;
  1673	- unredacted credential-bearing URLs.
  1674	
  1675	### 15.4 Provider and sidecar trust
  1676	
  1677	- pinned version/hash;
  1678	- executable path shown in settings;
  1679	- bounded stderr ring;
  1680	- no Tauri IPC capability;
  1681	- explicit workspace roots;
  1682	- process group cleanup;
  1683	- update is a separate reviewed action;
  1684	- custom provider manifests require explicit trust and cannot silently inherit existing credentials.
  1685	
