  2796	## 20. Stop conditions and explicit user decision gates
  2797	
  2798	A stop condition is not automatically a user decision. The controller first returns a bounded
  2799	evidence or repair packet for routing, ownership, dirty-seam, capability, test, cleanup, and
  2800	implementation failures. U0 and U1 are resolved and nonblocking. U2 is conditional evidence,
  2801	not an up-front selection or a reason to pause independent lanes.
  2802	
  2803	### 20.1 Explicit user gates
  2804	
  2805	- **U0 — resolved, nonblocking:** Luna Fast is preferred. Request and report
  2806	  `service_tier: "fast"` when available; if the native API has no tier field, immediately continue
  2807	  with explicit `gpt-5.6-luna`, `max`, `fork_turns: "none"` and make no Fast claim. Missing or
  2808	  unreported Fast tier never pauses an implementation lane. Model and reasoning-effort overrides
  2809	  remain the previously approved routing contract.
  2810	- **U1 — resolved, nonblocking extension/API selection:** release new candidates classified as
  2811	  `Works now` or `Bounded adapter`. Preserve existing declarative assets, but skip new
  2812	  `Declarative only`, `Elevated host required`, and `Rejected` rows without blocking the wave.
  2813	  The comparison and R0 are evidence/review gates, not a new user-selection pause. A future exact
  2814	  third-party package/hash or elevated-host proposal remains separate deferred scope.
  2815	- **U2 — A0 architecture exception:** ask only if ACP or Browser feasibility contradicts a locked
  2816	  top-priority behavior or requires a new native, packaging, trust, or security architecture. A
  2817	  successful A0 creates no ceremonial pause.
  2818	
  2819	If live TSK-808 is already closed, continuation requires explicit user revival; do not reopen it
  2820	or keep implementing from historical plan text.
  2821	
  2822	### 20.2 Controller stop and repair conditions
  2823	
  2824	Stop the affected lane, preserve evidence, and do not release dependents when:
  2825	
  2826	- the required Luna Max or SOL-medium model/effort route is unavailable, rejected, or downgraded;
  2827	- refreshed `origin/main`, current task state, or a protected merged checkpoint cannot be safely
  2828	  attributed;
  2829	- a packet needs an unlisted or controller-owned file, overlaps an active lease, or the controller
  2830	  cannot attribute its diff;
  2831	- more than two heavy build/test runners would overlap;
  2832	- A2 has not passed its contract tests before any A3 provider or A3-terminal lane starts;
  2833	- provider capability/config values would be guessed, hard-coded, or shown without effect;
  2834	- image input, load/resume, subagent parent identity, cancel/close, cleanup, or no-hidden-TUI
  2835	  behavior cannot be demonstrated;
  2836	- structured/native handoff cannot prove one writer, rollback, and exact history reconciliation;
  2837	- workflow scheduling/recovery would parse agent prose or bypass worktree, concurrency, budget,
  2838	  permission, output-schema, or file-lease policy;
  2839	- delegation would gain arbitrary process, path, Git, worktree, credential, executable, or IPC
  2840	  authority;
  2841	- Paneview/Dockview migration would create a second layout/store authority or lose persisted state;
  2842	- Browser clipping, profile/capability isolation, snapshot/overlay safety, exact ownership, or
  2843	  cleanup fails;
  2844	- resource/process ownership cannot be revalidated or provider quota would be guessed;
  2845	- assistance would silently mutate, block, or bypass preview/confirmation/revalidation/audit;
  2846	- CodeLens/Peek counts, editor identity, or tab-strip visibility changes without an attributable
  2847	  trace;
  2848	- SQL aggregation, grouping, filtering, joins, sorting, or paging would occur in memory, generated
  2849	  SQL cannot be inspected, or an N+1/load-then-loop path remains;
  2850	- focused, full, or native proof cannot be run, attributed, and cleaned up.
  2851	
  2852	If one of these conditions requires U2, the review card contains exact alternatives, evidence,
  2853	security/resource consequences, and a recommended choice for the affected lane. Independent lanes
  2854	continue. Otherwise route the bounded repair under section 16's model manifest without
  2855	interrupting the user.
