docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md-38-
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md:39:Workflow transitions are full structured run snapshots in additive `workflow.*` rows in that same ledger. `WorkflowReducer` is pure: ordered rows reduce to the latest run snapshot and set the replayed sequence. Appends share one process writer lock with legacy appends. Workflow appends allocate `max(sequence)+1`, deduplicate `(runId,idempotencyKey)`, and compare the snapshot's expected `lastSequence` with the current sequence before writing. A stale writer receives a typed ledger error and cannot overwrite a newer transition.
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md-40-
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md-41-## Determinism and policy
--
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md-44-- Input JSON is canonicalized by sorted object keys and frozen with a stable FNV-1a 64-bit hash.
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md-45-- Ready nodes are ordered lexically and become ready only when all dependency and edge predecessors are completed or skipped.
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md:46:- Global, per-workflow, and per-provider active counts are checked before dispatch.
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md-47-- Depth, attempts, wall time, node timeout, tokens, tool terminals, and worktree allocations produce `WorkflowError::BudgetExhausted(WorkflowFailure)`; the associated failure transition is appended where the run/node changes state.
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md-48-- Retry requires a failed node, remaining node/role/workflow attempts, and a role-allow-listed failure code when the role declares retryable codes.
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md-49-- Failure descendants are cancelled when `cancelDescendantsOnFailure` is enabled.
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md-50-- Phase is derived from run/node state plus the active node's configured role; input/result prose is never inspected.
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md:51:- Gate approval requires `{ approved: boolean }` structured input.
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md-52-- Results must deserialize into the named receipt structure. A string, hostile prose, missing fields, or wrong field types is refused.
docs/superpowers/evidence/tsk-808/a6-workflow-engine-receipt.md-53-- Active worktree/file leases are reconstructed from replayed node state. Overlapping write paths in one cwd are rejected. Dispatch cannot bypass the lease port.
--
